# ---- Data: never commit the Home Credit dataset ----
data/*
!data/sample/
!data/sample/**
!data/.gitkeep

# ---- Model artifacts ----
# The trained model IS committed. It is 6MB, it was fitted on the full
# 307,511-row dataset which cannot itself be committed, and without it a fresh
# clone would silently retrain on synthetic fixtures and report different
# numbers from this README. Shipping it means the app serves the real model
# immediately -- no training step, no waiting.
models/*
!models/.gitkeep
!models/*.joblib
!models/*.json
!models/*.csv
!models/*.npy

# ---- Generated reports ----
# Metrics and CSVs are regenerated by the pipeline and stay out of git. The
# figures ARE committed: the README embeds them, the presentation uses them,
# and someone browsing the repo should see the analysis without running
# anything. Note the directory has to be un-ignored before a rule can match
# files inside it -- git does not descend into an excluded directory, which is
# why an earlier `!reports/figures/*.png` on its own did nothing.
reports/*
!reports/.gitkeep
# Metrics from the real-data run, so the README's numbers are verifiable from
# the repo and the UI can show them before anything has been run.
!reports/*.json
!reports/*.csv
!reports/*.txt
!reports/figures/
reports/figures/*
!reports/figures/*.png
!reports/figures/.gitkeep

# ---- Secrets ----
.env
.env.local
*.pem
*.key

# ---- Python ----
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
venv/
.venv/
env/
ENV/
.python-version

# ---- Tooling caches ----
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.DS_Store

# ---- Jupyter ----
notebooks/.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ---- Streamlit ----
.streamlit/secrets.toml

# Streamlit secrets are per-deployment and never committed; the config is.
.streamlit/secrets.toml
